  "question": {
    "text": "<p>An electron of a hydrogen like atom, having <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, jumps from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></math> energy state to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></math> energy state, The energy released in this process, will be: (Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>V</mi></math>)</p><p>Where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo></math> Rydberg</p><p>constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math>Speed of light in vacuum</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo></math> Planck&#39;s constant</p>",
